The function `bpf_prog_test_run_xdp()` calculates `max_data_sz` as the maximum allowable data size, but it then calls `bpf_test_init()` with this maximum size instead of the size specified by the user. This leads to a situation where the function attempts to copy more data than the user intended, resulting in sporadic `EFAULT` errors when the actual data size exceeds the expected size.

